              "id": "CVE-2026-55685",
              "name": "CVE-2026-55685 in react-router 7.15.1 (unauthenticated manifest endpoint DoS)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-55685 in react-router 7.15.1 (unauthenticated manifest endpoint DoS)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The desktop client pins `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom` and is therefore within the affected version range for `CVE-2026-55685`. The advisory describes an unauthenticated manifest endpoint denial of service issue that is fixed in `7.18.0`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The desktop client pins `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom` and is therefore within the affected version range for `CVE-2026-55685`. The advisory describes an unauthenticated manifest endpoint denial of service issue that is fixed in `7.18.0`.\n\nIf the affected React Router server/runtime path is reachable in this application or in a bundled dependency path, unauthenticated requests can trigger excessive manifest processing and degrade availability.\n\nUpgrade `react-router-dom` and its resolved `react-router` dependency to `7.18.0` or later, then regenerate the lockfile so the desktop client no longer resolves the vulnerable version.",
                "markdown": "The desktop client pins `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom` and is therefore within the affected version range for `CVE-2026-55685`. The advisory describes an unauthenticated manifest endpoint denial of service issue that is fixed in `7.18.0`.\n\nIf the affected React Router server/runtime path is reachable in this application or in a bundled dependency path, unauthenticated requests can trigger excessive manifest processing and degrade availability.\n\nUpgrade `react-router-dom` and its resolved `react-router` dependency to `7.18.0` or later, then regenerate the lockfile so the desktop client no longer resolves the vulnerable version."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.7",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CVE-2026-55685",
                  "stride:T",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53666",
              "name": "CVE-2026-53666 in react-router 7.15.1 (client-side constructor execution information disclosure)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53666 in react-router 7.15.1 (client-side constructor execution information disclosure)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The desktop client resolves `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom`, which is inside the affected range for `CVE-2026-53666`. The advisory describes information disclosure via client-side constructor execution and is fixed in `7.18.0`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The desktop client resolves `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom`, which is inside the affected range for `CVE-2026-53666`. The advisory describes information disclosure via client-side constructor execution and is fixed in `7.18.0`.\n\nIf the vulnerable client-side routing path is exercised, attacker-controlled navigation data can disclose information through constructor execution in the browser context.\n\nUpgrade `react-router-dom` and the resolved `react-router` dependency to `7.18.0` or later, then refresh the lockfile to eliminate the vulnerable version.",
                "markdown": "The desktop client resolves `react-router` `7.15.1` through `react-router-dom`, which is inside the affected range for `CVE-2026-53666`. The advisory describes information disclosure via client-side constructor execution and is fixed in `7.18.0`.\n\nIf the vulnerable client-side routing path is exercised, attacker-controlled navigation data can disclose information through constructor execution in the browser context.\n\nUpgrade `react-router-dom` and the resolved `react-router` dependency to `7.18.0` or later, then refresh the lockfile to eliminate the vulnerable version."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
